continue doing that.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.410
Another pattern that I
think is pretty common

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:36.490
in cloud, but not other places,
is you build up the whole disk

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:40.270
image, including the software,
and then call that version A.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.483
And then you build
up another disk image

00:07:42.483 --> 00:07:44.650
with a new version of
software, call that version B.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.170
And then you can rotate that
into one of these groups

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.762
and upgrade that way.

00:07:48.762 --> 00:07:50.470
And if something goes
wrong, you can just

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.852
go back to the old image.

00:07:51.852 --> 00:07:53.560
CARTER MORGAN: This
is why I'm convinced,

